WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.640
Good morning John. I'm in a Target.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.800
And I'm tired.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.460
And I don't feel good.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:07.580
But here I am.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.580
I'm going to have to figure out something to do for the next 15 hours

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:13.540
and I really hope that it's at least a little bit interesting.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.220
[piano music]

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.700
I've been in Target for about five hours now,

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.300
and I am REALLY BORED.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.300
[laughing tiredly]

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.320
There's not a lot to do here.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.060
[ribbit ribbit ribbit]

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.420
[air blowing]

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.260
Hey, Nerdfighters came to see me.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.620
Why am I here?

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.800
Oh now this is just. Why?

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:15.540
Why, why do you put yogurt in the workout section?

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:18.580
Nice, warm yogurt. Good job consumer.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:20.780
Aside from being an excellent ninja mask,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.760
this balaclava is good for staying warm in the cold Montana winter.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.860
However, they didn't call it a balaclava, they called it a baclava.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.460
I feel like a little bit of a jerk for complaining about my punishment,

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:33.900
when you didn't really do anything and you have to get a root canal today.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.720
Though as you pointed out, you did break the basic rules of dental hygiene.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.040
This is why every year for our entire lives, our Mum has bought us a toothbrush.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.420
And what? Did you just ignore that?

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.820
There are lots of people in this Target and they, they don't think I'm normal.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.240
[Impersonating FRED] Hey, it's Haaaaaaank.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.660
[Impersonating FRED] Oh my gosh, you guys I've been in Target for twelve freaking hours.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:15.920
Katherine just came to hang out with me at the Target,

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.920
and we have been doing a lot of math in this candy aisle,

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.700
to try and figure out what candy is the worst for you.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.200
We're doing that by figuring out what has the most calories per gram.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.460
For a long time we thought it was going to be Reese's Peanut Butter Cups,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.720
and then we thought it was going to be the Dove Peanut Butter Cups,

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:34.380
but it turns out that it's the Lindor Peanut Butter Truffles,

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.120
with 5.9 calories per gram.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.120
More expensive too, you get what you pay for,

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:41.920
which is chubby.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.240
[pitch getting progressively higher] Ah, ah, ah, ah!

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.680
[4 voices together] Ahhhhh!

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.360
One last heaping spoonful.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.160
[coughing]

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.780
It's a horrible idea, you suck.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:22.760
John, you have to face your fear of heights and go on the Froghopper for a full froghop session,

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.100
and while you're up there, I want you to tell me you love me.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.220
John, see ya on Friday.

